  <atlas:FormalSystemDefinition rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/entry/mobus-revisions-oct-tuple">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mobus (2025), revisions manuscript, eq. (1)</rdfs:label>
    <atlas:statedIn>
      <cco:ont00000253 rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/bearer/mobus-book-revisions">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mobus, G. E. — Revisions to Systems Science: TAMD (working manuscript, March 2025, shared with Halcyonic)</rdfs:label>
        <dcterms:creator>George E. Mobus</dcterms:creator>
        <atlas:authoredBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/author/george-mobus"/>
        <dcterms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear">2025</dcterms:date>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Quoted with the author's permission, granted 2026-08-19 (video call).</rdfs:comment>
      </cco:ont00000253>
    </atlas:statedIn>
    <atlas:sourceLocation>"Extending and Modifying the Framework", eq. (1), revising Eq. 4.1 of the 2022 book</atlas:sourceLocation>
    <atlas:verbatim>Revised Eq. 4.1 is as follows.
Sᵢ,ₗ=⟨C,N,E,G,B,T,H,Δt⟩ᵢ,ₗ (1)
In what follows, the subscript indexes, i, for index number in the set, and l, for level in the complexity/organization hierarchy will be dropped for simplicity.
S is now given as an oct-tuple with new member E containing the set, O, (standing for "objects" in the environment that are sources and sinks in a unified set) and a new object, M, containing the non-point source/sink variables constituting the interacting milieu around the system.</atlas:verbatim>
    <atlas:displayForm>Sᵢ,ₗ=⟨C,N,E,G,B,T,H,Δt⟩ᵢ,ₗ</atlas:displayForm>
    <atlas:displayContext>S is now given as an oct-tuple with new member E containing the set, O, (standing for "objects" in the environment that are sources and sinks in a unified set) and a new object, M, containing the non-point source/sink variables constituting the interacting milieu around the system.</atlas:displayContext>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/set">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">set</skos:prefLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Signature role (D1, 2026-08-18): deliberately unassigned — ambient set theory — the metalanguage the definitions are written in, not a symbol of any signature. Not a gap; a verdict.</rdfs:comment>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/environment">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">environment</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Bunge's E. Things outside the composition that act on, or are acted on by, components. Mobus's revised tuple (entry 007) also carries an E — absent from his published 2022 seven-tuple, which is why the row lights up only on the revisions entry: the difference records the revision.</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/sort"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/hierarchy">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">hierarchy</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Mobus's 'system-subsystem hierarchy'. Kept distinct from level-of-organization: the hierarchy is the structure, a level is a position in it.</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/relation"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/level-of-organization">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">level of organization</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Mobus's index l: 'the index l is the level of organization in the system-subsystem hierarchy.'</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/sort"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/object">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">object</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Mobus's O, 'standing for "objects" in the environment that are sources and sinks in a unified set' (revisions manuscript, eq. 1).</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/sort"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/milieu">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">milieu</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Mobus's M, 'the non-point source/sink variables constituting the interacting milieu around the system' (revisions manuscript, eq. 1).</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/sort"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:invokesPrimitive>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/primitive/time">
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/PrimitiveScheme"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">time</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Bunge's triple is indexed at a time t. Klir's is not. A candidate point of divergence. In Bertalanffy's eq. (3.1) the invocation is notational — the t of dQᵢ/dt — rather than the word. Mobus's Δt (Eq. 4.1) is likewise notational at the definition; the word arrives only in the tuple's elaboration.</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:broader rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/role/sort"/>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:invokesPrimitive>
    <atlas:formalisedAs>Systems/Category/ShapeMobus.lean#MobusShape</atlas:formalisedAs>
    <atlas:evidenceCode>
      <atlas:EvidenceCode rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/MDHC">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">model-drafted, human-checked</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model produced the encoding; a human checked it against the verbatim text.</skos:definition>
      </atlas:EvidenceCode>
    </atlas:evidenceCode>
    <atlas:encodedBy>claude-opus-5 via atlas/ingest/draft_entry.py; checked by Shingai Thornton (guided pass)</atlas:encodedBy>
    <atlas:encodedOn rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-18</atlas:encodedOn>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">VERIFIED AS MDHC: model-drafted by the P5 pipeline and checked by Shingai
Thornton 2026-08-18 in the same guided session as entry 006 — verbatim, spans, primitives,
caveat and date each ruled on. The manuscript date (March 2025) was supplied by Shingai, who
received the document from its author.

DELIBERATELY NOT ASSERTED: cco:ont00001808 (is about), per the neutrality invariant.

THE REVISION IS THE FINDING. Entry 006's tuple has seven coordinates; this one has eight,
and the new coordinate is E — the environment, now carrying the source/sink objects O and
the milieu M. The environment becoming first-class is the same move Bertalanffy made between
1968 and 1972 (environment_is_new in the Lean development), which makes this the catalogue's
second revision arc with the same content. prim:environment lights up on this entry and not
on entry 006 by design: the census row difference IS the record of the revision.

PRIMITIVES (ruled 2026-08-18): the conservative standard, the words of the passage itself —
set, environment, hierarchy, level of organization, object, milieu — plus time notationally
via Δt (the dQᵢ/dt precedent, as on entry 006). "System" is deliberately NOT recorded as a
primitive: it is the definiendum, the term the definition fixes, not an undefined input it
rests on — and a row every entry would trivially share carries no census information.

NO AUTHOR CAVEAT (ruled 2026-08-18): the drafted candidate ("the subscript indexes ... will
be dropped for simplicity") is notational bookkeeping, not a self-qualification. The
manuscript's framing sentence — that the 2022 treatment "ignored a critical aspect of real
systems, namely that they age and change" — qualifies the OLD definition, and belongs to
this arc note rather than to a caveat on the new one.

HELD, NOT ENTERED: the manuscript's lifecycle equations (St+1 = St⟨ΔS⟩ with
ΔS = ⟨ΔC,ΔN,ΔE,ΔG,ΔB,ΔT,ΔH⟩) were scanned as a candidate. They introduce typed components
and fix a transition relation, but they define system CHANGE over an already-given S rather
than the term "system" — held pending a spec §5 ruling. They are the natural formal locus of
the Mobus life-cycle work and the Bunge–Mobus change-convergence thread, and likely enter
through the mapping layer rather than as an entry.

FORMALISATION: MobusShape encodes THIS equation ("Book-revisions Eq. 1" in
Systems/Mobus/Tuple.lean), which is why the pointer sits here and not on entry 006.</rdfs:comment>
