    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">DELIBERATELY NOT ASSERTED
No cco is-about relation is asserted between this entry and any subject matter, in keeping with the catalogue's neutrality invariant: the entry records that Joslyn writes this definition at this locus, not that the definition is about control, systems, or any worldly phenomenon.

SOURCE AND RENDERING
The verbatim is taken from the 2026-08-27 page-image transcription prefacing the file, which the transcriber marks as the authoritative text for formula-bearing quotes because the PDF's own text layer carries systematic subscript and ligature damage ("controlj" for control₁, "controlg" for control₂, "constrainedj" for constrained₁) and flattens the printed angle brackets ⟨ ⟩ to parentheses. Subscripts appear as Unicode subscript digits, as in the transcription; the printed page carries them as typeset subscripts. This is an MDU draft: the human pass should check the rendered subscripts and brackets against the page image.

NOT ENCODED
display_context is null: Definition 28 has no immediate authorial gloss inside the transcribed section, and the explication that follows on pp. 103–104 ("Control2 requires a bit of explication and exemplification. First, we recognize that O varies over a state space...") survives only in the damaged body layer, so it could not be given as an exact substring of a page-faithful verbatim. Likewise not encoded: the dependence of this definition on Definition 25 (control₁), Definition 15 (constraint₂) and Definition 6 (constraint₁), which the entry leaves as lexical primitives rather than unfolding; the derivation at Proposition 29 that O in a control₂ system must itself decompose as ⟨O_E, O_I⟩; the mapping to Marken's Definition 27 (control_M) recovered as a special case; and the two complementary re-decompositions CS₁ and CS₂ of §3.7. The case verbatims are drawn from the damaged body text and reproduce its OCR spellings ("controlg", "constraintj", "Cs", "control2", "controlled2") exactly as the file carries them.

AUTHOR CAVEAT
None recorded: Joslyn qualifies the whole enterprise as semiformal and deliberately iterative in §1, and remarks before Definition 28 that Marken's control is "adapted to our terminology, and generalized slightly," but no qualification is placed on this definition itself in a form that could be lifted verbatim as a caveat on it.</rdfs:comment>
