        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The source's form can redescribe the target; nothing need be preserved. Vacuously satisfiable by design — mapping 001 shows every catalogued definition passes, and that the constraints distinguishing the target are exactly what redescription is permitted to discard. A claim in this relation is deliberately weak evidence of anything.</skos:scopeNote>
      </skos:Concept>
    </atlas:claimRelation>
    <atlas:claimSource>
      <atlas:FormalSystemDefinition rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mathematical-systems/atlas/entry/klir-2001-eq-1-1">
