        <atlas:verbatim>S = (T, R),   (1.1)

where S, T, R denote, respectively, a system, a set of things distinguished within S, and a relation (or, possibly, a set of relations) defined on T. Clearly, the thinghood and systemhood properties of S reside in T and R, respectively.</atlas:verbatim>
